A '''sourhog''' is a boar-like monster introduced in [[A Porcine of Interest]]. It requires [[reinforced goggles]] to kill, or a [[Slayer helmet]] after the quest. If no protection is worn, the caustic saliva they spit will burn the player's eyes, draining the player's current [[Attack]] and [[Defence]] by 90% and cause 20-30 damage each hit accompanied by the player exclaiming {{overhead|Argh! My eyes!}}. Sourhogs are aggressive to players regardless of their combat level.

According to [[Spria]], the sourhog was created when two farmers competed in a competition each year, with the same farmer winning each year. The other farmer, who was jealous of his rival, hired a dark wizard to alter one of his pigs, turning it into the Sourhog.{{CiteNPC|npc=Spria|quote=Many years back, before even I was around, there were two rival family farms not far from where we're standing. Every year the village would hold a 'Finest Swine in Show' prize at the annual faire. The same farmer would win year after year without fail. Driven mad with jealousy, his rival decided to hire a dodgy dark wizard to give him an edge over the competition. The wizard attempted to alter the pig's appearance. I'm sure you can guess how well that went!|loc=A Porcine of Interest|notes=|name=}} This sourhog escaped and successfully bred more of its own kind.{{CiteNPC|npc=Spria|quote=Long story short, the mutant, what we now know as a Sourhog, went on a brief rampage and escaped. It must have somehow managed to reproduce, because people have reported seeing them in groups.|loc=A Porcine of Interest|notes=|name=}} Sourhogs prefer to live in underground caves and in primitive tribes.{{CiteNPC|npc=Spria|quote=Rumors are, they live in deep underground caverns, scavenging what they can find.|loc=A Porcine of Interest|notes=|name=}}


